    <string name="about_taps_title">Taps not working?</string>
    <string name="about_taps_body">Android draws normal overlays below the status bar, so touches on the island never reach it. Turn on the Islandify accessibility service: it only draws the island above the status bar and does not read your screen.</string>
    <string name="about_btn_accessibility">Accessibility</string>
    <string name="about_stopping_title">If the island keeps stopping</string>
    <string name="about_kill_brand">%1$s phones kill background apps. Do these three things:</string>
    <string name="about_kill_generic">Some phones (Xiaomi, Oppo, Vivo, Realme, Samsung) kill background apps. If the island stops, do these three things:</string>
    <string name="about_step1">1. Battery: no restrictions.</string>
    <string name="about_step2">2. Autostart ON (Xiaomi/Oppo/Vivo).</string>
    <string name="about_step3">3. Lock Islandify in the recent apps screen.</string>
    <string name="about_btn_battery">Battery</string>
    <string name="about_btn_guide">Guide</string>
    <string name="onb_a11y_why">Lets the island sit above the status bar so it can receive taps. Islandify only draws the island and does not read your screen. If the switch is greyed out: App info &gt; menu &gt; \"Allow restricted settings\", then come back.</string>
    <string name="onb_listener_why">Lets the island see messages, calls and music. If the toggle is greyed out: App info &gt; menu &gt; \"Allow restricted settings\".</string>
    <string name="onb_post_why">Needed to show the small \"Islandify is running\" notification that keeps the island alive.</string>
    <string name="onb_bt_why">Lets the island show the name of your earbuds when they connect.</string>
    <string name="onb_battery_why">Phones like Xiaomi, Oppo and Samsung kill background apps. This stops them from closing the island.</string>
    <string name="onb_title">Islandify setup</string>
    <string name="onb_intro">Grant the permissions below once. After that the app opens and the island starts by itself.</string>
